---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import LessonIllustration from "../../components/LessonIllustration.astro";
import MapStructureDemo from "../../components/MapStructureDemo.astro";
import StructureFacts from "../../components/StructureFacts.astro";
import TermCallout from "../../components/TermCallout.astro";
import { sharedMapTerm } from "../../lib/atlas/standalone-terms";
import "../../styles/set-lesson.css";
---

<BaseLayout title="SharedMap" description="The ranger numbers competing gate-status notes in a shared notebook." territory="Structures" sheetTitle="SharedMap">
  <article class="register-lesson">
    <header class="page-intro">
      <p class="territory-label">Structures</p>
      <h1>SharedMap</h1>
      <p class="structure-summary">
        The ranger gives each hiker a notebook with a line for the gate status.
        Alice writes "Trail open" and Bob writes "Trail closed" before either
        sees the other's note.
      </p>
      <LessonIllustration id="structures-shared-map" />
    </header>
    <StructureFacts structure="SharedMap" family="DDS" model="Sequenced operation-based map" updates="Write, cross out, or clear named entries" merge="Use the last numbered change for each name." delivery="One server-ordered operation stream" bestFor="Shared JSON settings with one service to number changes" cost="Accepted entries plus notes awaiting a number" />
    <section aria-labelledby="order-title">
      <h2 id="order-title">The ranger numbers each change</h2>
      <p>
        In a <dfn><a href="/glossary/#sharedmap">SharedMap</a></dfn>, the ranger
        numbers every accepted change. When two hikers change the same line,
        the higher number decides what all three notebooks show.
      </p>
      <p>
        Alice sees her own note as soon as she writes it. She keeps it in her
        notebook while she waits for the ranger's number. Even if Bob's note
        arrives first, Alice still sees her own answer until the ranger sends
        back the numbered changes.
      </p>
      <TermCallout {...sharedMapTerm} />
      <figure><table aria-label="SharedMap gate-status race"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Ledger number</th><th scope="col">Note</th><th scope="col">Gate status</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">1</th><td>Alice · Trail open</td><td>Trail open</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">2</th><td>Bob · Trail closed</td><td>Trail closed</td></tr></tbody></table><figcaption>The ranger's ledger number, not the time on a note, decides which answer stays.</figcaption></figure>
    </section>
    <MapStructureDemo kind="shared-map" title="Number two gate-status notes" description="Alice and Bob write on the gate-status line before they see each other's note. The ranger numbers Bob's change last." rule="Use the highest ledger number for each line." raceLabel="Race the two gate-status notes" />
    <section aria-labelledby="limit-title"><h2 id="limit-title">One answer survives</h2><p>The ranger's rule leaves one answer on the line; the other disappears. If dates on offline notes should choose the answer, use LWWMap. If a new note must survive a crossed-out line, use OR-map.</p></section>
    <section aria-labelledby="source-title">
      <h2 id="source-title">Sources and implementation</h2>
      <p>
        <strong>Sources:</strong> Watershed's{" "}
        <a href="https://github.com/tylerbutler/watershed/blob/4a8739323ee491f353fcaa8ccfb0488419c1cd43/src/watershed/map_kernel.gleam">SharedMap kernel</a>.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Implementation:</strong> The demo calls Watershed through the Gleam toolkit
        and connects three clients in a <a href="/glossary/#sluice">Sluice</a> room.
        The server sequence selects the value for each key.
      </p>
    </section>
    <nav class="structure-next" aria-label="Continue through map structures"><a href="/structures/maps/">Back to map family</a><a href="/structures/lww-map/">Continue to LWWMap</a></nav>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
